      "$comment": "THE TOP OF THE SPEED CATALOGUE, REACHED BY A SHIPPED BUILDING FOR THE FIRST TIME. elevator-specs.json's ultra-high-speed class is {min 10.0, max 20.5, typical 10.0} and its 20.5 is taken from this very machine (realWorldAnchors: 'Shanghai Tower 20.5 World's fastest (Mitsubishi)'), and until this bank no building in data/buildings/ went faster than 10.0 -- so the top half of the class's own range had a UI caller (authoring/machineSpec.ts's ceiling, which a player can already dial) and no content caller. GitHub issue #424, and its own correcting comment, which is why this is stated as 'no authored example' rather than as a dead seam. cabinPressurised is CHOSEN and is the one field here with a source behind it: elevator-specs.json's airPressure $comment records Al-Kodmany (Buildings 2015) noting that THIS TOWER answers the air-pressure problem with a pneumatic system. Without it a 418.5 m bank would cap this car's descent at 10.0 m/s and the fastest lift in the catalogue would come down at the speed of the slowest supertall shuttle in the set; with it the machine is symmetric at 20.5 m/s both ways, which is what makes this tower the SYMMETRIC arm beside ctf-class-reference's asymmetric one.",
