  "notes": [
    "Six banks and 106 cars over a 568 m rise, against burj-class-reference's six banks and 57 cars over 596 m. That contrast is the point of the building and it is a contrast in DENSITY rather than in height: four local banks of twenty cars each, where the Burj-class tower's locals run eight to eleven. GitHub issue #424 asks for 'a denser bank arrangement over a shorter rise, which is a different point in the design space and not a bigger version of it'.",
    "The observation deck is a populated floor and its visitors are not modelled, which is stated rather than left to be discovered. Floor 119 carries 30 people -- the deck's own staff and its restaurant -- so it is a real origin and a real destination on the office-standard profile and the hotel bank really serves it. What this repository has no template for is the VISITOR crowd an observation deck draws, which is GitHub issue #436's subject; authoring a separate observation express here would have been a bank almost nobody rides, which is DECISIONS.md SS D265's defect rather than fidelity.",
    "Every car states passengerTransferS, because data/buildings/README.md refuses to default one on a mixed-use building. The shuttle takes the hotel's 1.5 s rather than the offices' 1.2 s on the README's own rule -- where a bank carries more than one population the slower value is chosen -- because it is the only route to the hotel and a guest with luggage is aboard it every trip. No new reference value is authored.",
    "The stage cannot draw this tower legibly and that is recorded rather than implied. docs/12 SS 4.16 measured the SS 7 stage on the shipped bundle at 35 legible floors at 1280x800 and 40 at 1440x900; this building has 129. It is in exactly the position burj-class-reference is in, for the same reason, and GitHub issue #377 owns the remedy."
  ]
